A||||3||BENGAL4||VALVE COVER GASKETS
Z||000000||BENGAL4||08-09-99||06:42 AM||||I just finished painting the plenum and valve covers and all the part stores seem to carry are the  intake & plenum gaskets but nobody stocks the valve cover gaskets. Are they reusable? They are made of some type of rubber and seem to be in good shape. Just wondering if someone else has run into this problem.<br>
Z||000001||batboy||08-11-99||06:46 PM||||I have reused valve cover gaskets that looked good before. A thin (light) coat of silicone engine sealer (Permatex or similar) on both sides of the gasket ought to seal it up one last time.
Z||000002||Dad of 5||08-23-99||04:22 PM||||I just found one at Trak Auto in the D. C. area for a 84 4 cylinder.  They are out there.
Z||000003||lowCG||08-23-99||10:59 PM||||Just bought a set(Fel-Pro,VS50077R)look like a nice set of gaskets,thick,rubber,triangle profiled o-ring style gaskets that sit in a groove in the valve covers,I wouldn't recommend siliconing them.<br>
